  "title": "COVID-19, Influenza, and RSV Wastewater Monitoring in the U.S. | Week of April 25, 2026",
  "summary": "Summary: Week of 4/25/26 Respiratory viruses are continuing to move in the right direction. Across Biobot’s national wastewater network, every major virus we track is declining nationally and in every region, including SARS-CoV-2, influenza A and B, RSV, and HMPV. That is great news. But we’re not all the way back to low-season levels […]",
